i was just thinking about how in the previous implementation K was always 0.9988... i.e. the filter was believing
everything the sensor said, whereas in this one K converged to 0.013 i.e. the filter didn't believe anything the sensor
said (glancing at the output file the accelerations appear in kalman_integrate appear to be much smaller than in
base_integrate), but the result ended up the same (the velocities and positions are very similar). but then I realized I
put the wrong data in - R is the variance of the measurement i.e. of the accelerometer data, but I set it to the
variance of the jerk during the calibration period.

----
now fixed:
    [nibawr@amaranth py]$ ./scratch ../../pulled/rec_20260708_205242.csv 20 > slide-kalman3-y.json
